{"binId":"codex-on-Justo", "details":"Governance + future-proofing audit. (A) Ruling bodies mapped: 20 statutes and standards (ACL ss 29/51/54/56/259, Evidence Act 1995 (Cth) s 79, Evidence Act 1995 (NSW) s 177, Federal Court of Australia Act s 31 + FCR Pt 23, Corporations Act Pt 2M.3 + s 286-342, ASIC Act, Privacy Act + APPs, FOI Act, NVETR Act, Trade Marks / Copyright / Patents Acts, AASB/IFRS, ISO/IEC 27001/27037/27042, IEC 62443, DO-178C DAL A, IEC 61508, ARINC 653, Common Criteria). (B) Client hardening verified: all 16 timestamps UTC, monotonic clock for TauFirewall, UTF-8 explicit on every file IO, sort_keys + compact separators on every Merkle-relevant json.dumps, no locale, zero urllib/requests/http.client imports, no API_KEY/TOKEN/secrets, all request bodies validated by Pydantic, paths stripped with Path(name).name in batch_download and _safe_filename in report_writer. (C) Future-proofing: PROJECT_VERSION + DECEPTION_ONTOLOGY_VERSION as single-source constants, schema_version=1.0 field recommended on next block, Merkle chain is hash-only so v1.0.0 chains verify in v1.1.0, schema-bump ritual documented (bump version -> seal CONSTANTS_BUMP -> re-run tests -> changelog entry -> update GOVERNANCE/DECEPTION_ONTOLOGY). External deps all local-only. Sealed as block 216, Merkle root a11119e3811b61b0576ec069647c9df00e8d7b926250b5a411a6e6aad88b2d83, chain still verifies.", "summary":"Ruling-body map + client hardening + future-proofing audit sealed to chain.", "timestamp":"2026-07-11T19:48:07Z", "type":"governance_audit"}
