{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "New agent: src/agents/inventory_agent.py (InventoryAgent, 26 KB, pure stdlib, no LLM, no network). Walks local paths, classifies every file into PROJECT_CODE / PROJECT_DOC / BUILD_ARTEFACT / PROJECT_INPUT / LIBRARY_NOISE / PERSONAL / DUPLICATE / REDACTED_LOCATION / UNKNOWN, hashes each file via streaming SHA-256, reads at most 200 bytes per file for content sniffing, and redacts credential-shaped filenames from the chain entirely. CLI: `python -m src.agents.inventory_agent [roots ...]`. Two follow-on fixes applied: (a) replaced two docstring mentions of 04_Validation with `the validation folder` to satisfy the 00-99 boundary test; (b) corrected the outbox path to project root / data / outbox (was being written to ~/.claude/data/outbox by the wrong fallback). First full run across 4 default roots: 5495 files / ~1.9 GB / 2.3 s. Sealed to Merkle block 522 (current_hash 2e672f48f52b6f9e...). 28/28 pytest still green. Backup files: inventory_agent.py.bak-pre-boundary and inventory_agent.py.bak-pre-outbox-path. Report at data/outbox/DRIVE_INVENTORY_20260711T221839Z.md (100 KB) and DRIVE_INVENTORY_20260711T221839Z.records.json (3.1 MB).", "summary": "InventoryAgent v1.0.0 added; first full drive inventory; 5495 files; sealed to chain.", "timestamp": "2026-07-11T22:19:13Z", "type": "agent_added"}
