{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "timestamp": "2026-07-12T03:40:36Z", "type": "change", "summary": "Closed OPEN_ITEMS step 4 (reset-registry foot-gun) + B2 (determinism regression test). Fixed latent POST /api/facts bug.", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 close (layer 1). (1) Fixed the real foot-gun: Orchestrator.__init__ was calling reset_registry() and re-seeding 3 facts on EVERY HTTP request to /api/orchestrator/process, because the orchestrator was instantiated per-request. The orchestrator now leaves the facts registry alone. (2) Made _seed_facts() work in TestClient: extracted into _seed_facts_once() with a _SEEDED module flag, called from BOTH the startup event (for uvicorn) and from /api/facts (for TestClient where @app.on_event(\"startup\") is unreliable). (3) Fixed latent bug: POST /api/facts was using Fact (7-field) instead of FactCreate (3-field), so the endpoint was unusable. Switched to FactCreate. (4) Added test_orchestrator_does_not_wipe_operator_facts -- posts a unique-marked fact, calls orchestrator, asserts the fact is still there. Verified the test catches the original bug. (5) Added test_evaluation_suite_is_deterministic -- runs /api/eval/run 3 times, strips runId+timestamp (only volatile fields), asserts byte-identical. Closes B2. Tests: 32/32 pytest green (was 30, +2). No-network audit: 39/39 CLEAN. Sealed as block 1392, current_hash c2b85178dfe134f4835214a41d9ca61fbacc65bc0fd59b001f5448c204c91207, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root b5dc0411 (1391 blocks). Files changed: 02_Technical/src/server/app.py, 02_Technical/src/agents/orchestrator.py, tests/test_smoke.py. Open items remaining: A1, A4, A5, B1, B3, B4, C1-C5, D1, D5."}
{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 (layer 2). Migrated 02_Technical/src/server/app.py from deprecated @app.on_event(\"startup\") to the modern @asynccontextmanager-based FastAPI lifespan handler. (1) Added from contextlib import asynccontextmanager. (2) Added async def _lifespan(app: FastAPI) that calls _ensure_seeded() at startup, no-op shutdown. (3) Wired lifespan=_lifespan into the FastAPI() constructor. (4) Removed the @app.on_event(\"startup\") decorator and the _seed_facts() function it wrapped. The lazy _ensure_seeded() guard in /api/facts is kept as belt-and-suspenders for non-standard test harnesses. Side effect: the DeprecationWarning on_event is deprecated, use lifespan event handlers instead no longer fires on pytest runs (was 3 warnings, now 0 from this path; 1 unrelated httpx2 warning remains from Starlette). Tests: 32/32 pytest green. No-network audit: CLEAN. Sealed as block 1683, current_hash 825151c03f577430f46ac68c14b748e9356788fbd8162903b2848d9774963252, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root 7bbe4fac (1682 blocks). Files changed: 02_Technical/src/server/app.py. app.py sha256 b2617e7dcb1b5a683571cadc8b7fc09827187da04c0b39c36dadd3bcc43896d1. Open items remaining: A4, A5, A6, B1, B3, B4, C1-C5, D1, D5.", "summary": "Closed OPEN_ITEMS A1 (lifespan migration). on_event deprecation gone.", "timestamp": "2026-07-12T03:50:00Z", "type": "change"}
{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 (layer 2, A6). The OPEN_ITEMS doc entry A6 (line 68) was already correctly diagnosed as a documentation note, not a code issue: the .pyc cache is regenerated by Python on every import and any mismatch is a no-op. The fix is preventative: (1) added a project-root .gitignore covering __pycache__/, *.pyc, *.pyo, *.pyd, .pytest_cache/, .vscode/, .idea/, .DS_Store, Thumbs.db, and standard virtualenv dirs. (2) Deleted 6 stale __pycache__ directories under 02_Technical/{config,src,src/agents,src/engines,src/io,src/server} (excluded tauri-shell, which is a JS/TS subproject with its own .gitignore at 02_Technical/tauri-shell/.gitignore). (3) Deleted 02_Technical/.pytest_cache/. After cleanup: pytest 32/32, no-network audit CLEAN exit 0, chain MATCH. Pytest re-populated __pycache__ as expected; the .gitignore keeps them out of any future git add. Sealed as block 1800, current_hash 96425dc07912b099cc6850276b02230872c07b8db477031c6e131fe23a274e6d, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root 55cffb23 (1799 blocks). .gitignore sha256 50793f7e5ec31002a36015cc62e74b4c497dd8fbd7a1206f951aae48e5acd312. Open items remaining: A4, A5, B1, B3, B4, C1-C5, D1, D5.", "summary": "Closed OPEN_ITEMS A6 (stale .pyc cache). Added project-root .gitignore; deleted existing __pycache__ and .pytest_cache directories.", "timestamp": "2026-07-12T03:55:00Z", "type": "change"}
{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 (layer 2, A4 prebuild). (1) Spec audit: read all 8 Tauri source files end-to-end (Cargo.toml, tauri.conf.json, package.json, build.rs, src/main.rs, src/lib.rs, src/commands.rs, capabilities/default.json) plus web/index.html. 3 latent issues found: (a) bundle.targets included Linux/macOS targets the host cannot build -- fixed to [msi, nsis]. (b) longDescription hardcoded 52-pattern -- refreshed to 54-pattern + v3.9 + explicit no-network-runtime. (c) capabilities/default.json granted shell:default, dialog:default, fs:default even though the front-end never calls those plugins -- tightened to core permissions only. (2) Generated 6 valid placeholder icon files (32x32, 128x128, 128x128@2x, 512x512 PNG, valid .ico, valid .icns) with project brand color #1f3a3d. These are placeholders; operator should swap in real designed icons before public release. (3) Pre-build file hashes snapshotted to 02_Technical/tauri-shell/A4_PREBUILD_HASHES.json for audit replay. (4) Rust 1.97.0 stable installed via rustup-init.exe (12.8 MB installer, ~90 sec, pre-existing .rustup/settings.toml re-used). cargo --version OK. (5) Blocked: Windows C++ toolchain (MSVC linker + Windows SDK) is NOT installed. where link.exe returned Git Bash coreutils link (not MSVC), where cl.exe empty, where gcc empty, gcc --version command not found. Tauri build will fail at link time. Three options for operator: O1 MSVC Build Tools via winget (recommended, ~3 GB, ~15 min), O2 MinGW-w64 + rustup GNU target (~500 MB, ~8 min, has known Tauri plugin edge cases), O3 defer A4 (Python runtime is production path, Tauri is the USB fallback). Sealed as block 1859, current_hash 10acc6f4a29ccd535c8ffaeafaa945fa196d73db145fa311c8c1f7ac7810cba8, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root bea527a7 (1858 blocks). 32/32 pytest still green. No-network audit still CLEAN. Open items remaining: A4 (blocked on MSVC, operator decision), A5, B1, B3, B4, C1-C5, D1, D5.", "summary": "OPEN