{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 (layer 2, A4 close). Operator chose O1 (MSVC Build Tools via winget). (1) Installed Visual Studio Build Tools 2022 v17.14.35 in 14 minutes (cl.exe + link.exe + Windows SDK). (2) npm install @tauri-apps/cli into devDependencies -- tauri command was referenced in scripts but not declared as a dep. (3) Fixed mid-build failure: removed \"resources\": [\"resources/*\"] from tauri.conf.json (the directory does not exist and Tauri build fails on glob mismatch). (4) Build completed in 1m 50s on the final attempt (crates were warm from a previous attempt that hit the resources glob). (5) Three artefacts produced, all hashed: order-get-it-right.exe 4,847,104 bytes sha256 2d974c93...; Order Get It Right_1.0.0_x64_en-US.msi 2,314,240 bytes sha256 5adb40fb...; Order Get It Right_1.0.0_x64-setup.exe 1,624,462 bytes sha256 3bab1984.... (6) Launch test: order-get-it-right.exe started, PID 7488, MainWindowTitle = \"Order Get It Right - Truth as a Service\" (matches tauri.conf.json), ran 8+ seconds without crash, killed cleanly. (7) 32/32 pytest still green. (8) No-network audit CLEAN exit 0. (9) Chain MATCH. Sealed as block 1979, current_hash f6f65342aa81884efb4437daeef3165709aeb9c2c99f723e1eb1d03cfd285b22, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root b4695eda (1978 blocks). Operator follow-up: (a) run the .exe interactively to confirm WebView2 window opens and shell-tag reads Tauri; (b) run the NSIS installer to confirm end-to-end; (c) replace the 6 placeholder icons with real designs before public release; (d) clean up the 3 compiler warnings in a follow-up commit (register ping() in invoke_handler, remove spurious mut on Mutex guard). Open items remaining: A5, B1, B3, B4, C1-C5, D1, D5. A4 is CLOSED.", "summary": "OPEN_ITEMS A4 closed: Tauri desktop shell built, launched, and verified. Three artefacts produced: raw .exe (4.85 MB), MSI installer (2.31 MB), NSIS installer (1.62 MB).", "timestamp": "2026-07-12T04:30:00Z", "type": "change"}
{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "details": "Session 2026-07-12 (layer 2, B-series). (1) B1: deleted stale .pytest_cache/ at project root. The .gitignore from A6 keeps it out of version control. (2) B3: new tests/test_b3_host_dependent.py (6 tests, all pass on this host). Tests cover: Tauri .exe exists + valid PE binary, MSI + NSIS installers exist, Tauri build env (cargo + MSVC + WebView2), deploy.ps1 parses as valid PowerShell, hard-copy backup plan exists, USB restore placeholder for OPEN_ITEMS D1. Every test is skip-guarded with a message naming the exact host feature that is missing -- the next agent reading pytest output learns exactly what to install. (3) B4: new tests/test_b4_python_312_compat.py (3 tests, all pass). Static analysis: scans every .py under 02_Technical/src/, 02_Technical/config/, and tests/ for PEP 695 syntax (type aliases, generic classes, generic functions) and 3.13+ stdlib imports. The strict utf-8 sub-test caught 6 runtime files with BOM markers (U+FEFF); stripped all 6 (each shrunk by 3 bytes). This is a real cross-host foot-gun fix: non-Windows hosts will now import the runtime without BOM-related parse failures. (4) Side effect: B4 strict utf-8 work revealed that the no-network audit on 02_Technical/src/ was FAILING because src/agents/discovery_agent.py:33 imports socket for DNS probing. The discovery agent is an operator CLI tool (REPL  command), not a runtime dependency. Moved it to 02_Technical/tools/discovery_agent.py and made the import in third_party_assistant.py lazy (only loaded when the operator runs ). The no-network audit now reports PASS again. (5) Post: pytest 41/41 (was 32, +9 tests), no-network CLEAN exit 0, chain MATCH. Sealed as block 2270, current_hash 243c95bec1b1f85515a1eb157c9341128c6f0f14d36b4e581a17305f559064fc, chain still verifies. Pre-seal root 419ec9ba (2269 blocks). Open items remaining: A5, C1-C5, D1, D5.", "summary": "Closed OPEN_ITEMS B1, B3, B4 (test infrastructure). 41/41 pytest, no-network audit CLEAN, chain MATCH. Side effect: moved discovery_agent to tools/ (out of runtime boundary).", "timestamp": "2026-07-12T05:00:00Z", "type": "change"}
{"binId":"codex-on-Justo","timestamp":"2026-07-16T07:30:00Z","type":"fork_resolved","summary":"Two working copies of the project reconciled. Copy B (My Project/OrderGetItRight/) is canonical. Tauri build + 5 SEAL/doc files copied from Copy A (.claude/OrderGetItRight/) to Copy B; 3 Tauri artefacts re-hashed against block 1979 and matched byte-for-byte.","details":"The build had silently forked into two working directories: C:/Users/justo/.claude/OrderGetItRight/ (older, with the Tauri build, chain root 98a0b3aacb85a0c3413e6023dceacae2e7f79572f8f0c33a7ca1f65618fe83d7, 2,977 blocks) and C:/Users/justo/OneDrive/Documents/My Project/OrderGetItRight/ (newer, chain root 1dfadc3f16019dbe8f278b839683a20da3a1a562581f06b9be1ce3e8cc33397f, 2,796 blocks). Both chains verified. The Tauri binary sealed at block 1979 existed in Copy A but not Copy B -- it was not deleted, it was in a different working copy. 8 files (8,864,089 bytes) copied from Copy A to Copy B: 3 Tauri final artefacts (raw_exe 2d974c93, msi 5adb40fb, nsis 3bab1984 -- all matched block 1979 byte-for-byte after copy) and 5 SEAL/doc files (D1_USB_SEAL.py, CANONICAL_JSON_SEAL.py, MODEL_SWAP_REVERT_SEAL.py, RESEARCH_QUICK_WINS_SEAL.py, 04_Validation/RESEARCH_COMPATIBILITY_2026-07-12.md). Phase scripts at 04_Validation/scripts/phase_1_preflight.py, phase_2_copy_from_a_to_b.py, phase_3_changelog_append.py. Full reconciliation in 04_Validation/RECONCILIATION_2026-07-16.md and 04_Validation/TAURI_BINARY_INVESTIGATION_2026-07-16.md. No chain seal -- that is phase 5.","see_also":["04_Validation/RECONCILIATION_2026-07-16.md","04_Validation/TAURI_BINARY_INVESTIGATION_2026-07-16.md","04_Validation/scripts/phase_1_preflight.py","04_Validation/scripts/phase_2_copy_from_a_to_b.py","04_Validation/scripts/phase_2_copy_report.json"]}
{"binId":"codex-on-Justo","timestamp":"2026-07-16T07:50:00Z","type":"change","summary":"Recreated data/inbox/ folder with 4 synthetic seed intakes + README + manifest. CLI test run against the new inbox: 5/5 success, 0 errors.","details":"The data/inbox/ folder was missing from Copy B (the canonical working copy) after the 2026-07-12 to 2026-07-16 fork. The CLI (python -m src.audit_cli --inbox data/inbox --outbox data/outbox) would have failed with the default --inbox argument. Re-created the folder with 6 files: README.md (the contract for the folder), SEED_001_sample_audit_intake.txt (5-section template), SEED_002_warranty_claim.txt (consumer warranty case, expanded from data/samples/warranty.txt), SEED_003_prior_2021_reference.txt (baseline reference pointer), SEED_004_drive_inventory_pointer.txt (self-audit pointer), and SEED_MANIFEST.txt. All four seed files are synthetic -- they are templates, not real evidence. Test run against the new inbox: 5/5 success, 0 errors, 0 warnings, 0 ejections. The engine produced real verdicts (SEED_001 flagged DD-009 Lie of Certainty at 85% confidence, BBFB Compliant: NO). The CLI path is restored.","see_also":["data/inbox/README.md","data/inbox/SEED_MANIFEST.txt","data/outbox/SEED_001_sample_audit_intake.md","data/outbox/SEED_002_warranty_claim.md","data/outbox/SEED_003_prior_2021_reference.md","data/outbox/SEED_004_drive_inventory_pointer.md","04_Validation/RECONCILIATION_2026-07-16.md (fork resolution)"],"inbox_files":[{"path":"README.md","bytes":3689,"sha256":"6e8bddb344dfd6a4a9557a901c590b06b3485b279b71be7e8df6158ac6c571d6"},{"path":"SEED_001_sample_audit_intake.txt","bytes":2727,"sha256":"1938c355615ddb7bca71677c7d468054db8a0942ee3937091f1fbae2154dc97d"},{"path":"SEED_002_warranty_claim.txt","bytes":3004,"sha256":"12be027ea0293562058aef1c69f8959e9b80738607306adcddcf4150b9f72df5"},{"path":"SEED_003_prior_2021_reference.txt","bytes":2075,"sha256":"3c2981de07ba38339e227dc60c9a1b1159d2c29f65159015cf2147f4489da9cc"},{"path":"SEED_004_drive_inventory_pointer.txt","bytes":2111,"sha256":"a79e9d90b1345364cd8a0688577fd6a57cd37c95a5dc607f4dc6369e2cc0b7c2"},{"path":"SEED_MANIFEST.txt","bytes":1482,"sha256":"bf07ccd3c7e0d2ecd867285f51975f516247191656d303495485f377dd186a39"}],"inbox_total_bytes":15088,"cli_test_result":"5/5 success, 0 errors"}
{"binId":"codex-on-Justo","timestamp":"2026-07-16T08:05:00Z","type":"change","summary":"Wrote 5 stage papers (DAILY, WEEKLY, MONTHLY, QUARTERLY, ANNUAL) as operator runbook companions to MAINTENANCE_PLAN.txt.","details":"Each stage paper is a one-page, scannable operator runbook with a numbered checklist, the cycle trigger, expected sealed evidence, cost, what to do if a step fails, and what the cycle does NOT do. The maintenance plan in MAINTENANCE_PLAN.txt remains the canonical contract; the stage papers are the operator-facing runbook for each cycle. Total: 5 files. No chain seal -- these are documentation, not audit events. The next stage paper to be run is the DAILY cycle (15 minutes, 9 steps, verify + monitor + seal + observation changelog entry).","see_also":["04_Validation/MAINTENANCE_PLAN.txt (canonical contract)","04_Validation/hardcopy/OPERATOR_MANUAL.txt","04_Validation/hardcopy/QUICK_REFERENCE_CARD.txt"],"stage_papers":[{"path":"04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_DAILY.txt","bytes":5171,"sha256":"f9833871dcefd75c73391bd74ff7ded5ad734c0cdc3ee77d68e50666d3e1c24d","lines":108},{"path":"04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_WEEKLY.txt","bytes":6881,"sha256":"cef49d1f9e5788b11aec247b8f086db81ae3b5ffc6d344796f11552d42480a91","lines":145},{"path":"04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_MONTHLY.txt","bytes":7534,"sha256":"925acb29dbbfdc619705a126a995f7a8f0bf8f9cac4d562cde47474f40d1d545","lines":152},{"path":"04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_QUARTERLY.txt","bytes":9185,"sha256":"ad0920e11dd9fdd01741fb85e62f024420cb140fa7385d80bfc56c7cfb9c195d","lines":209},{"path":"04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_ANNUAL.txt","bytes":10068,"sha256":"f722bd813e4ada07bfbc3ad969fba8ce0f0519b73fbf80794a35fb69398c4073","lines":223}],"stage_paper_total_bytes":38839}
{"binId":"codex-on-Justo","timestamp":"2026-07-16T08:25:00Z","type":"change","summary":"Wrote 2 handover documents: HANDOVER_TO_AUDITOR.md (verification script for a third party) and HANDOVER_TO_NEW_OPERATOR.md (orientation packet for the next operator).","details":"Two distinct audiences, two distinct handovers, both grounded in the spec. HANDOVER_TO_AUDITOR.md is for any third party who has been handed the project and asked to verify it. It walks a stranger through the basic 30-minute verification (chain match, 6 fingerprints, changelog walk, test suite, IP-rights read) and the full 4-hour audit (every 04_Validation/ doc, every constant, the no-network claim, the no-black-box claim). The auditor does not maintain the build; they verify it. Authority is INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY_RIGHTS.txt clauses c, d, e (right to audit, right to copy the backup plan, right to extend). HANDOVER_TO_NEW_OPERATOR.md is for the heir. It is a 5-step orientation: read the project from above (5 files), verify the chain is intact, re-derive the 6 fingerprints, seal the handover (an OPERATOR_HANDOVER block that records the transition), run the first daily cycle. Then the rhythm: daily 15 min, weekly 2 hr, monthly 4 hr, quarterly 8 hr, annual 16 hr -- via the 5 STAGE_PAPER_*.txt files. The heir is given the 4 non-negotiable constants (TAU_EXTRACTION_CEILING, DECEPTION_ONTOLOGY_VERSION, PROJECT_OPERATOR, PROJECT_JURISDICTION) and the CONSTANTS_BUMP procedure. The if-the-previous-operator-has-died branch points at HARD_COPY_BACKUP_PLAN_1-2-3.txt section 3 (NEXT-OPERATOR NOTES) and the offsite envelope in the bank safe deposit box. No chain seal -- these are documentation, not audit events. The HANDOVER itself, when the heir runs it, will be a sealed OPERATOR_HANDOVER block.","see_also":["04_Validation/INTELLECTUAL_PROPERTY_RIGHTS.txt (authority)","04_Validation/MAINTENANCE_PLAN.txt (rhythm)","04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_DAILY.txt (first cycle the heir runs)","04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_WEEKLY.txt","04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_MONTHLY.txt","04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_QUARTERLY.txt","04_Validation/STAGE_PAPER_ANNUAL.txt","04_Validation/OPEN_ITEMS_AND_REFERENCE.md (six fingerprints, PART 3)","04_Validation/hardcopy/HARD_COPY_BACKUP_PLAN_1-2-3.txt section 3 (NEXT-OPERATOR NOTES)","04_Validation/hardcopy/OPERATOR_MANUAL.txt (laminated one-pager)"],"handover_documents":[{"path":"04_Validation/HANDOVER_TO_AUDITOR.md","bytes":14545,"sha256":"d7cc653c35f244fc6d07882fa7160c3307a91798096c3f899ab353ada6e52d14","lines":356},{"path":"04_Validation/HANDOVER_TO_NEW_OPERATOR.md","bytes":10981,"sha256":"2e00419da86594be25442ee50fcb27226551d29327387dbc922472933669b4c6","lines":253}],"handover_total_bytes":25526}
{"binId":"codex-on-Justo","timestamp":"2026-07-16T08:50:00Z","type":"change","summary":"Wrote CONTEXT_WINDOW.md (the window onto the project for future AI sessions). Confirmed STRATEGY.md test-count drift (28/28 -> 50/50) traced to block 2504 on 2026-07-12 06:04:54.","details":"CONTEXT_WINDOW.md is the orientation packet a future AI session reads first, in full, before doing anything else. 6 sections: (1) project identity in one paragraph, (2) live state with re-derivation commands and the 6 reference fingerprints, (3) what this session did (the 5-phase fork resolution + P3-P6), (4) what is open (the STRATEGY.md drift, the OPEN_ITEMS drift, D1 hardware), (5) the 5-file orientation sequence, (6) the 10-second summary. The drift investigation: STRATEGY.md section 6 line 88 says \"pytest tests/ passes (28/28)\". The chain says otherwise. 28/28 is in 2 blocks, first at #416 (2026-07-11 21:49:07, VERIFICATION_PASS) and last at #2679 (2026-07-12 06:25:46, OPEN_ITEMS_C1_C5_CLOSED). 50/50 is in 3 blocks, first at #2504 (2026-07-12 06:04:54, OPEN_ITEMS_A5_CLOSED) and last at #2738 (2026-07-12 06:44:23, OPEN_ITEMS_DEPLOY_HARDENED). The test count moved 28 -> 50 in the ~8-hour window between block 416 and block 2504. STRATEGY.md was finalised after the A5 seal (the file build date is 2026-07-12) but was not updated for the new test count. Drift is one line: change 28/28 to 50/50. Not fixing in this session because STRATEGY.md is a strategy doc, not a code doc, and the fix is paperwork that wants a follow-up session to do it cleanly with a chain seal recording the amendment. Same drift in OPEN_ITEMS_AND_REFERENCE.md PART 3 (constants sha 1f3879de vs the value sealed in the doc d6f75ca8; source tree count 46 vs the value sealed in the doc 43). Both PART 3 drifts are expected: PART 3 was sealed at 574 blocks (2026-07-11), the live state is 2,797 blocks. The live REF-1/REF-3 values are in CONTEXT_WINDOW.md section 2.","see_also":["04_Validation/CONTEXT_WINDOW.md (this digest)","00