{"binId": "codex-on-Justo", "timestamp": "2026-07-17T10:35:00Z", "type": "change", "summary": "A3 closed: POST /api/facts now calls _ensure_seeded() before adding the operator fact.", "details": "The seed-on-POST gap was the residual foot-gun. _seed_facts_once() was already guarded by , but the POST /api/facts handler did not call _ensure_seeded() on a fresh process. Modern FastAPI TestClient does not fire the lifespan handler before the first request, so the first operator POST in a fresh process would land in a registry with no seed facts (the test that was supposed to close A3 was failing on this exact assertion). Fix: POST /api/facts now calls _ensure_seeded() before adding the operator fact. _seed_facts_once() guard ensures no operator-fact wipe. Test reinforced: forces a clean baseline, asserts seed categories are present before the operator add, asserts operator id is not a seed id, asserts re-seed does not duplicate, asserts second re-seed is idempotent. test_smoke.py 28/28 pass; full suite 76 pass + 1 skip (D5 E2E)."}
